From: daxiaamu ColorOS 17 8T port
Subject: [PATCH] f2fs: retain unmount discard timeout with OF2FS enabled

The OF2FS conditional introduces a new else-if before the upstream
timeout assignment. With OF2FS enabled, DPOLICY_UMOUNT consequently
retains the common timeout=false initialization. Restore the timeout
in the unmount branch, leaving the OF2FS balance/performance behavior
unchanged. Existing pending-discard cleanup remains responsible for
dropping unissued work and waiting for submitted requests.

Observed on the 8T OS17 first boot after fastboot -w: init spends hundreds
of seconds in f2fs_put_super -> f2fs_issue_discard_timeout ->
__issue_discard_cmd. Two independent SysRq-l CPU snapshots identify
the same path. Keep encryption and normal mounted discard enabled.

Base: OnePlusOSS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8250
Commit: 846e71f228ad605c75b53064c4c165a1361a0bfe

--- a/fs/f2fs/segment.c
+++ b/fs/f2fs/segment.c
@@ -1349,6 +1349,7 @@
 	} else if (discard_type == DPOLICY_UMOUNT) {
 		dpolicy->io_aware = false;
 		/* we need to issue all to keep CP_TRIMMED_FLAG */
 		dpolicy->granularity = 1;
+		dpolicy->timeout = true;
 #ifdef CONFIG_OPLUS_FEATURE_OF2FS
 	} else if (discard_type == DPOLICY_BALANCE ||
